<title>USA: DC Intertie power line down, seen back up by Thurs.</title>
<headline>DC Intertie power line down, seen back up by Thurs.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The DC segment of the Pacific Intertie, which has a capacity of 3,100 megawatts (MW), was shut down Wednesday afternoon after a crane came in contact with the line, a spokeswoman for the Bonneville Power Administration.</p>
<p>The DC (direct current) line runs between the Pacific Northwest and Southern California.</p>
<p>The line was expected to be back in service by late Wednesday or Thursday morning.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761))</p>
